# The Tseitin ladder with observer bookkeeping disabled via the language's
# `unobserved:` block (global depth -- propagates into the solver).
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS (2026-08-11, EigenScript#915 / GAPS.md): the runtime computes
# observer entropy on every assignment even though this solver never reads an
# observer. Measured on 4x4: 299.95s observed vs 34.73s here (8.6x), counters
# byte-identical (conflicts=9986 resolutions=33873) -- the wrapper captures the
# entire measured ceiling of the ungated cost. Search is provably unaffected:
# every lane preflight gates on byte-identical counters between this harness
# and the devbox bank.
#
# Per the repo rule ("don't bypass an EigenScript gap silently"), BOTH paths
# stay: benchmarks/tseitin_ladder.eigs is the observed baseline, this is the
# comparison. The systemic fix (gate the default) is upstream as #915.
#
# Usage: eigenscript benchmarks/tseitin_ladder_unobserved.eigs <rows> <cols> [progress_s]
unobserved:
    load_file of "benchmarks/tseitin_ladder.eigs"
